<title>INDIA: Indian sugar market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Indian sugar market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bombay sugar market was closed on Thursday for a national holiday. It will reopen on Friday.</p>
<p>On Wednesday ready sugar S-30 rose 30 rupees to 1,390/1,420 rupees per quintal and M-30 gained 10/15 rupees to 1,420/1,487 rupees per quintal. On Tuesday S-30 sugar prices rose 10/15 rupees and M-30 by 9.0/10 rupees per quintal.</p>
<p>&quot;The market is very firm in anticipation of surge in demand,&quot; said a dealer.</p>
<p>-Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
